+7.49 KVM_CAP_S390_USER_EXT_IRQ
+------------------------------
+
+:Architectures: s390
+:Type: vm
+:Parameters: args[0] - control register 0 bits (external-interruption
+             subclass masks)
+:Returns: 0 on success; -EINVAL if args[0] is zero, another argument is not
+          zero, or the VM has the KVM_VM_S390_UCONTROL flag set.
+
+With this capability user space can present external interruptions that it
+emulates itself, for instance those of a hypervisor service that the guest
+calls with an instruction user space handles (see
+KVM_CAP_S390_USER_OPEREXEC). args[0] holds the bits of control register 0
+that enable these interruptions. The capability can be enabled again with
+other bits.
+
+Such an interruption is injected with KVM_S390_IRQ and the type
+KVM_S390_INT_EXT_USER::
+
+  struct kvm_s390_ext_user_info {
+	__u64 subclass;
+	__u16 code;
+	__u16 cpu_addr;
+	__u32 params;
+	__u64 params2;
+	__u32 flags;
+	__u32 reserved;
+  };
+
+  #define KVM_S390_EXT_USER_CPU_ADDR	0x01
+  #define KVM_S390_EXT_USER_PARAMS	0x02
+  #define KVM_S390_EXT_USER_PARAMS2	0x04
+
+subclass holds the bits of control register 0 that enable the interruption,
+a non-empty subset of args[0]. KVM presents the interruption when the vCPU
+is enabled for external interruptions and at least one of these bits is one,
+after the other external interruptions that are pending and enabled. It
+stores code as the external-interruption code, cpu_addr as the CPU address
+if flags has KVM_S390_EXT_USER_CPU_ADDR, params as the external-interruption
+parameter if flags has KVM_S390_EXT_USER_PARAMS, and params2 at the location
+of the second parameter if flags has KVM_S390_EXT_USER_PARAMS2 and the vCPU
+is in z/Architecture mode. The PSWs are swapped in the format of the
+architectural mode. reserved must be zero.
+
+A vCPU holds at most one interruption of this type; KVM_S390_IRQ returns
+-EBUSY while one is pending. KVM_S390_GET_IRQ_STATE and
+KVM_S390_SET_IRQ_STATE include it. The type is not available for protected
+vCPUs.
+
 8. Other capabilities.
 ======================
 
